    {"id":"MORE-01","name":"Malabar Hill Reservoir repair and alternate tank","shortName":"Malabar Hill reservoir","summary":"In June 2024 the BMC dropped its plan to rebuild the 1887 Malabar Hill Reservoir after protests from residents over tree felling. IIT-Roorkee found the reservoir could be repaired, with an additional tank of about 52 million litres needed to repair it in phases. In September 2026 the Standing Committee appointed IIT-Roorkee to review a revised three-tier, 52-million-litre tank on an adjoining site, which cuts the trees to be felled from 389 to 82. Repair work has not started.","sector":"Water & sanitation","agency":"BMC","status":"Delayed","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null,"note":"The reconstruction plan approved in February 2022 was estimated at Rs 698 crore (FPJ). No cost has been published for the repair and alternate tank. IIT-Roorkee's review fee is Rs 22 lakh."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"FPJ reports that residents opposed tree felling and the loss of the Hanging Garden, so the reconstruction plan was dropped in June 2024. Since then the BMC has redesigned the alternate tank and sought IIT-Roorkee reviews.","areas":["Malabar Hill","Hanging Gardens","Walkeshwar"],"constituencies":["Malabar Hill"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/bmc-seeks-iit-roorkee-review-for-new-malabar-hill-reservoir-plan-after-tree-loss-reduced-by-307","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-09-24","claim":"Standing Committee approved IIT-Roorkee review (Rs 22 lakh fee) of a 52 ML three-tier alternate tank designed by Pednekar Associates; tree felling cut from 389 to 82; reservoir built in 1887"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-scraps-new-tank-proposal-saving-389-trees-and-iconic-hanging-garden-at-malabar-hill-reservoir","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2024-06-07","claim":"Guardian minister announced on 7 June 2024 that the new-tank/reconstruction proposal and tender would be scrapped after residents' objections; plan approved Feb 2022 at Rs 698 crore"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-malabar-hill-reservoir-reconstruction-scrapped-but-residents-worry-over-potentially-misleading-data-in-iit-r-report","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2024-08-20","claim":"Reconstruction scrapped after local opposition; IIT-Roorkee recommended an additional tank of over 52 ML to repair in phases"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.9567,"lng":72.8053},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-02","name":"Madh–Versova cable-stayed bridge over Malad Creek","shortName":"Madh–Versova bridge","summary":"A 2,064 m elevated bridge over Malad Creek, including a 600 m cable-stayed section, would link Versova and Madh Island. It would replace a road journey of about 21 km. APCO Infratech won the contract in 2024. Preliminary surveys and soil tests began in December 2025, and the Bombay High Court allowed the felling of 1,237 mangroves in September 2026. Main construction had not been reported as started.","sector":"Roads & bridges","agency":"BMC","status":"Not started","progress":null,"cost":{"original":2029,"revised":null,"note":"₹2,029 crore was APCO Infratech's winning bid against a ₹1,800 crore BMC estimate (Swarajya, Mumbai Live, Sept 2024); the approved cost was then reported as ₹3,246 crore. FPJ reported ₹3,990 crore (Nov 2025, including maintenance, casting-yard rent and cost-fluctuation provisions) and an estimate of about ₹2,395 crore (Dec 2025, June 2026). Figures conflict."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":"APCO Infratech","startDate":null,"targetDate":"2029-03","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"FPJ reports that the BMC waited for mangrove diversion approval and for clearances from the Union environment ministry and the Bombay High Court. MCZMA had earlier asked for alternative alignments, approving the revised design in February 2023. The Bombay Environmental Action Group opposed the BMC's High Court petition.","areas":["Versova","Madh Island","Malad Creek"],"constituencies":["Versova","Malad West"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/versova-madh-island-bridge-bombay-hc-clears-way-21-km-journey-to-shrink-to-15-km","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-09-09","claim":"HC allowed removal of 1,237 mangroves on 2.75 ha; bridge 2,064 m long; replaces a ~21 km road journey"},{"url":"https://swarajyamag.com/amp/story/infrastructure/mumbais-upcoming-cable-stayed-bridge-to-connect-madh-and-versova-in-five-minutes-completion-slated-for-2027","title":"Swarajya","date":"2024-09-12","claim":"APCO Infratech won with ₹2,029 crore bid; estimate rose from ₹1,800 crore to ₹3,246 crore; three-year completion"},{"url":"https://www.mumbailive.com/en/civic/versova-madh-cable-stayed-bridge-to-cut-down-travel-time-to-5-minutes-85706","title":"Mumbai Live","date":"2024-09","claim":"APCO Infratech successful bidder at ₹2,029 crore plus 24% cost-variation provision; approved cost ₹3,246 crore"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-infra-news-madhversova-bridge-project-moves-forward-as-bmc-begins-surveys-construction-likely-in-2-months","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-12-19","claim":"Preliminary surveys and soil investigations begun; ~₹2,395 crore; 600 m cable-stayed section; target March 2029"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-infra-update-bmc-begins-environmental-clearance-process-for-2395-crore-madhversova-bridge-project","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-06-29","claim":"~₹2,395 crore; 2,064 m with 600 m cable-stayed section; target March 2029; awaiting clearances"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/bmc-awaits-final-green-and-hc-clearances-for-3990-crore-madhversova-bridge-work-likely-to-begin-next-year","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-11-06","claim":"₹3,990 crore project awarded 29 Aug 2024 incl. maintenance, casting yard rental, cost fluctuation; awaiting mangrove, MoEF and HC clearances; MCZMA approved revised design Feb 2023"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.1395,"lng":72.815},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-03","name":"Dahisar River rejuvenation (sewage treatment plants, interceptors and riverfront works)","shortName":"Dahisar river revival","summary":"The BMC is building sewage treatment plants, about 4.4 km of sewer lines, interceptors and service roads along a 4.75 km stretch of the Dahisar River. In February 2026 the state told the Assembly that two treatment plants were complete and would start working by 31 March 2026. In April 2026 the 5 MLD plant at Indira Nagar and the 1.5 MLD plant at Sukurwadi were being commissioned. Union Minister Piyush Goyal inaugurated Phase 1 on 10 May 2026. An activist said the plants were not working, while a local corporator said he had seen them operating.","sector":"Flood control","agency":"BMC","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":246,"revised":null,"note":"BMC allotted Rs 246 crore, per FPJ (Dec 2024 and Apr 2026)."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":246}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":"2026-03-31","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Dahisar East","Dahisar West","Sanjay Gandhi National Park"],"constituencies":["Dahisar"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/buffalo-sheds-along-mumbai-rivers-to-be-shifted-to-curb-pollution","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-02-26","claim":"Two Dahisar STPs completed, to be operational by 31 March 2026; rejuvenation works expected to finish by March 2026"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/thane-bmc-secures-clearances-for-1192-crore-poisar-river-rejuvenation-project-delays-may-escalate-costs","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2024-12-18","claim":"BMC allotted Rs 246 crore for Dahisar river rejuvenation; retaining wall already built"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-union-minister-piyush-goyal-push-takes-246-crore-dahisar-river-revival-near-completion-with-infrastructure-upgrades","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-04-08","claim":"Rs 246 crore; 5 MLD (Indira Nagar) and 1.5 MLD (Sukurwadi) MBR plants civil/mechanical work complete, in commissioning; 4.75 km river stretch; ~4.4 km sewer lines and interceptors; service roads"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/union-minister-piyush-goyal-inaugurates-dahisar-river-project-for-third-time-in-a-decade-activists-allege-no-ground-work","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-05-11","claim":"Piyush Goyal inaugurated Phase 1 on 10 May 2026; activist says STPs not working, corporator says he saw them operating"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.229,"lng":72.878},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-04","name":"Poisar River rejuvenation: ten sewage treatment plants, interceptors and service road","shortName":"Poisar river revival","summary":"This Rs 1,192 crore project would build ten 33 MLD sewage treatment plants on the Poisar River in Kandivali, with sewer lines, 13 interceptors, a service road and wider banks. The contract includes 15 years of operation and maintenance. The BMC tendered it in 2019 and awarded it about two years before clearances arrived in December 2024. By February 2026 nine of the ten plants were under construction.","sector":"Flood control","agency":"BMC","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":1192,"revised":null,"note":"Officials warned that delays could raise costs."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"Tendered in 2019. Work waited for clearances from the environment ministry, the Mangrove Cell and the coastal zone authority, and for 2,267 encroaching hutments to be dealt with.","areas":["Poisar","Kandivali East","Kandivali West","Malad Creek"],"constituencies":["Kandivali East","Charkop"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/thane-bmc-secures-clearances-for-1192-crore-poisar-river-rejuvenation-project-delays-may-escalate-costs","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2024-12-18","claim":"Rs 1,192 crore; 10 STPs of 33 MLD each with 15-year O&M; 13 interceptors; clearances received; tender issued 2019; 2,267 hutments affected"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/buffalo-sheds-along-mumbai-rivers-to-be-shifted-to-curb-pollution","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-02-26","claim":"Nine of ten proposed Poisar treatment plants under construction"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.209,"lng":72.864},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-05","name":"Oshiwara and Walbhat rivers sewage treatment facilities","shortName":"Oshiwara & Walbhat rivers","summary":"As part of its programme to clean the western-suburb rivers, the BMC is building five sewage treatment facilities across the Oshiwara and Walbhat rivers in Goregaon and Jogeshwari. The state reported all five in progress in February 2026.","sector":"Flood control","agency":"BMC","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Oshiwara","Goregaon","Aarey"],"constituencies":[],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/buffalo-sheds-along-mumbai-rivers-to-be-shifted-to-curb-pollution","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-02-26","claim":"Five treatment facilities in progress across Oshiwara and Walbhat rivers; buffalo sheds along the rivers to be relocated"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.165,"lng":72.87},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-06","name":"Andheri Subway permanent flood-mitigation scheme","shortName":"Andheri subway flood fix","summary":"Andheri Subway floods 25 to 30 times each monsoon. In April 2026 the state told the BMC to fix it and asked IIT Bombay for a long-term solution. The options under study are diverting Mogra Nullah and building an underground water-holding tank. In June 2026 the BMC said even a Rs 500-600 crore system, about five times the size of the Milan Subway one, may only halve the waterlogging. An expert committee is still studying the options.","sector":"Flood control","agency":"BMC","status":"Not started","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null,"note":"None sanctioned. Estimates: Rs 197 crore earmarked for a parallel drainage channel (Feb 2026); over Rs 250 crore for diverting Mogra Nullah and over Rs 500 crore for a holding tank (Apr 2026); Rs 500-600 crore for the large system (June 2026). All per FPJ."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"No agreed technical solution (FPJ). Four drains meet at the site, officials say diverting the nullah alone may not fix it, and an underground tank would close the corridor for 18 months.","areas":["Andheri West","Andheri East","Mogra Nullah"],"constituencies":["Andheri West","Andheri East"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-says-600-crore-flood-control-plan-may-only-halve-waterlogging-at-andheri-subway-permanent-fix-elusive","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-06-13","claim":"Rs 500-600 crore system may cut waterlogging only ~50%; tank would need 18-month closure; subway floods 25-30 times a monsoon; expert committee studying options"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/maharashtra-govt-directs-bmc-to-fix-andheri-subway-flooding-before-monsoon-mogra-nullah-diversion-and-tank-plan-under-review","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-04-16","claim":"State directs BMC to fix subway flooding; Mogra Nullah diversion (over Rs 250 crore) and holding tank (over Rs 500 crore) under review; IIT Bombay report awaited"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/amp/mumbai/bmc-proposes-197-crore-drainage-channel-to-end-andheri-subway-flooding","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-02-27","claim":"BMC proposes Rs 197 crore drainage channel parallel to the subway"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.1197,"lng":72.846},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-07","name":"Byculla Zoo (Veermata Jijabai Bhosale Udyan) tunnel aquarium and exotic animal facility","shortName":"Byculla Zoo expansion","summary":"The BMC is adding a 50 m tunnel-view aquarium with 70 marine species to Byculla Zoo, along with an exotic animal zone of 18 immersive enclosures for species such as cheetahs, giraffes and zebras. The projects were held up by earlier delays and controversies. In March 2026 the BMC said work had picked up pace, with the aquarium due in December 2026 and the exotic facility within about two years.","sector":"Heritage & public spaces","agency":"BMC","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null,"note":"Aquarium about Rs 65 crore; exotic animal facility Rs 500 crore, with Rs 136 crore allocated in 2026-27 (FPJ, March 2026)."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":"2026-12","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"The BMC planned an aquarium at the zoo in June 2022, but the then tourism minister proposed one at Worli instead. The zoo plan was revived in February 2024 after the change of government (FPJ, Mar 2026). In February 2025 an MLA asked for the tender to be cancelled because only one bidder qualified (FPJ, Feb 2025).","areas":["Byculla","Rani Baug"],"constituencies":["Byculla"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-bmc-speeds-up-nahur-bird-park-byculla-zoo-aquarium-and-exotic-animal-facility-projects","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-03-07","claim":"Aquarium Rs 65 crore, target December 2026; exotic facility Rs 500 crore with 18 enclosures, Rs 136 crore in FY 2026-27, expected within two years"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-to-reassess-byculla-zoo-aquarium-project-after-mla-rais-shaikh-raises-concerns-over-tender-process-and-location","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-02-04","claim":"MLA Rais Shaikh sought cancellation of the aquarium tender after a single eligible bidder; Rs 65 crore estimate"},{"url":"https://www.mumbailive.com/en/infrastructure/tunnel-aquarium-at-byculla-zoo-set-to-open-in-2027-90798","title":"Mumbai Live","date":null,"claim":"Tunnel aquarium tendered March 2024, work orders in May; civic target early 2027; construction progressing (undated; superseded by FPJ Mar 2026 target of Dec 2026)"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.979,"lng":72.835},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-08","name":"Nahur exotic bird park (aviary), Mulund West","shortName":"Nahur bird park","summary":"The BMC is building an exotic bird park at Nahur, Mulund West, as a satellite of Byculla Zoo, with naturalistic aviaries, water bodies, veterinary and quarantine facilities, and visitor amenities. It needed the land reservation changed from garden to zoo. A groundbreaking ceremony was held on 14 December 2025. In March 2026 the BMC said work had gained momentum, with a December 2027 target.","sector":"Heritage & public spaces","agency":"BMC","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":266,"note":"Rs 266 crore, with Rs 40 crore allocated in 2026-27 (FPJ, Mar 2026). Earlier figures: a Rs 100 crore estimate (FPJ, Mar 2025) and Rs 166 crore in the 2025 construction tender (FPJ, Sept-Oct 2025)."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":"2025-12-14","targetDate":"2027-12","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"In March 2025 FPJ reported the project had been stuck for two years while the state Urban Development department considered changing the land reservation from garden to zoo. Late in 2023, consultant tenders for the project report drew one bid, then none, and had to be issued a third time (FPJ).","areas":["Nahur","Mulund West"],"constituencies":["Mulund"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-bmc-speeds-up-nahur-bird-park-byculla-zoo-aquarium-and-exotic-animal-facility-projects","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-03-07","claim":"Nahur bird park Rs 266 crore; Rs 40 crore in FY 2026-27; target December 2027; work gained momentum"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-bmcs-mulund-bird-park-project-delayed-for-2-years-awaiting-state-approval-for-land-reservation-change","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-03-15","claim":"Delayed two years awaiting change of reservation from garden to zoo; Rs 100 crore estimate; the 2013 Rs 150 crore proposal was for a Powai plot"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmcs-nahur-aviary-project-faces-bidder-drought-third-tender-issued","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2023-12-24","claim":"Consultant tender drew one bidder, then none; third tender issued"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-bmcs-nahur-bird-aviary-project-faces-cost-escalation-controversy-zoo-officials-deny-wrongdoing","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-09-05","claim":"Tender at Rs 166 crore vs earlier Rs 100 crore; activist alleges 66% escalation; zoo denies wrongdoing"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-bmc-receives-9-bids-for-166-crore-exotic-bird-park-project-at-nahur","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-10-04","claim":"Nine bids for Rs 166 crore project; contractor to build and maintain for two years"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-bmc-to-begin-construction-of-nahur-exotic-bird-park-in-mulund-groundbreaking-ceremony-on-december-14","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-12-13","claim":"Groundbreaking ceremony on 14 December 2025"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.155,"lng":72.948},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-09","name":"Metro Line 8 (Gold Line): CSMIA Mumbai airport to Navi Mumbai International Airport","shortName":"Metro 8 (airport link)","summary":"This metro line of about 35 km would link Mumbai's two airports. It would run underground for about 9 km from CSMIA Terminal 2 to Chheda Nagar, via Kurla/LTT, then on an elevated viaduct along the Sion–Panvel Highway through Mankhurd and Vashi to NMIA. The state approved it on 27 January 2026 as a PPP project to be implemented by CIDCO. In November 2026 CIDCO appointed a consultant to obtain environmental and statutory clearances, with construction targeted to start in March 2027, subject to approvals. No concessionaire has been reported as selected.","sector":"Metro rail","agency":"CIDCO","status":"Not started","progress":null,"cost":{"original":20000,"revised":null,"note":"Rs 20,000 crore estimate at DPR stage (Swarajya, Apr 2025). At state approval on 27 Jan 2026, FPJ's headline gave over Rs 22,000 crore and its text gave about Rs 17,000-18,000 crore. No single approved figure has been confirmed."},"funders":[{"name":"Government of India","type":"Central Govt","amount":null,"note":"20% equity (FPJ)"},{"name":"Government of Maharashtra","type":"State Govt","amount":null,"note":"20% viability gap funding (FPJ)"},{"name":"PPP concessionaire (to be selected)","type":"Private / PPP","amount":null,"note":"60% (FPJ)"}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Sahar (CSMIA T2)","Kurla","LTT","Chheda Nagar","Mankhurd","Vashi","NMIA"],"constituencies":["Andheri East","Kurla","Chembur","Mankhurd Shivaji Nagar"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/good-news-for-air-travellers-over-22000-crore-metro-line-8-project-from-csmia-to-navi-mumbai-airport-gets-govt-nod-know-details-here","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-01-27","claim":"Cabinet sub-committee approved 27 Jan 2026; 20% central equity, 20% state VGF, 60% PPP; ~35 km; ~9 km underground with 6 stations; LTT-Kurla link; headline 'over 22,000 crore', body Rs 17,000-18,000 crore"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/amp/mumbai/maharashtra-approves-metro-line-8-linking-mumbai-and-navi-mumbai-airports-cidco-advances-expansion-plans","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-04-18","claim":"CIDCO to implement on PPP; 35 km incl. 9.25 km underground; route CSMIA T2, Chheda Nagar, Kurla, LTT, Mankhurd, Vashi, Nerul, Belapur, NMIA"},{"url":"https://swarajyamag.com/amp/story/news-brief/dpr-for-metro-line-8-linking-mumbais-two-airports-almost-complete-cidco-to-float-tenders-soon-for-rs-20000-crore-project","title":"Swarajya","date":"2025-04-22","claim":"CIDCO implementing under PPP; 34.9 km; underground from CSMIA T2 to Chheda Nagar, elevated along Sion-Panvel Highway; Rs 20,000 crore"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/cidco-appoints-consultant-to-secure-environmental-clearances-for-35-km-mumbai-metro-line-8-connecting-csmia-nmia","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-11-13","claim":"CIDCO appointed Building Enviro Pvt Ltd as clearances consultant; PPP model; construction targeted March 2027 subject to approvals; no concessionaire named"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.099,"lng":72.874},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-10","name":"Mumbai One integrated mobility app and common QR ticketing","shortName":"Mumbai One app","summary":"Mumbai One is MMRDA's single app for QR tickets and journey planning across suburban rail, Metro Lines 1, 2A, 3 and 7, the Monorail, Navi Mumbai Metro, and BEST, TMT, NMMT, KDMT and MBMT buses. Prime Minister Modi launched it on 8 October 2025. In its first month it had over 3 lakh registrations and 7.15 lakh journeys. Season tickets and return journeys on suburban trains cannot be booked in the app.","sector":"Other","agency":"MMRDA","status":"Completed","progress":100,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"MMRDA","type":"State Govt","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":"2025-10-08","delayReason":null,"areas":["Mumbai Metropolitan Region"],"constituencies":[],"citywide":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.theweek.in/wire-updates/national/2025/10/08/bes22-mh-app-mumbai-one.html","title":"The Week (PTI)","date":"2025-10-08","claim":"PM launched Mumbai One; 11 operators listed; single QR ticket; suburban season and return tickets not available"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-one-app-records-3-lakh-registrations-enables-over-7-lakh-journeys-in-first-month","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-11-17","claim":"Over 3 lakh registrations and 7.15 lakh journeys in the first month; launched by MMRDA"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.064,"lng":72.865},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-11","name":"Redevelopment of 22 BEST bus depots under PPP (DBFOT)","shortName":"BEST depot redevelopment","summary":"BEST plans to redevelop 22 of its 27 bus depots into integrated hubs with staff housing and commercial and social infrastructure, while bus operations continue. Developers would build them under a design-build-finance-operate-transfer PPP while BEST keeps the land. The BMC General Body approved the plan at a session that ended just after midnight on 18-19 August 2026, over opposition from Congress and Shiv Sena (UBT). The file now goes to the Urban Development Department and the state Cabinet, then back to BEST and the BMC for final approval.","sector":"Other","agency":"BEST","status":"Not started","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null,"note":"Rs 28,000 crore is the amount BEST says it needs for long-term stability (employee commitments, debt servicing and buying and running 5,000 new buses), which the plan is meant to help fund. It is not a construction estimate (FPJ, Aug 2026)."},"funders":[{"name":"Private developers (PPP-DBFOT)","type":"Private / PPP","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["22 BEST depots across Mumbai"],"constituencies":[],"citywide":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-infra-update-bmc-clears-28000-crore-redevelopment-plan-for-22-best-depots-despite-opposition","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-08-20","claim":"General Body approved on 18 Aug 2026; PPP-DBFOT; BEST retains land; now goes to UDD and Cabinet; FSI hike from 1.3 to 7 sought"},{"url":"https://theprint.in/india/from-bollywood-icon-to-cash-strapped-utility-mumbais-red-buses-get-a-rs-28000-crore-rescue-plan/3022216/","title":"ThePrint","date":"2026-08-22","claim":"BMC general body approved redevelopment of 22 of 27 depots under PPP-DBFOT with BEST retaining land"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.923,"lng":72.832},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-12","name":"Worli Dairy land redevelopment as a commercial-financial hub","shortName":"Worli Dairy land","summary":"The state has given MMRDA ownership of the former government dairy site at Worli, about 15.8 acres (6.4 ha), to develop as a commercial-financial hub with residential and recreational uses. MMRDA expects the project to raise money for its metro work. Earlier plans for an aquarium and marine research institute may be dropped. Suggestions and objections were invited in September 2025. No development work has been reported.","sector":"Other","agency":"MMRDA","status":"Not started","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"MMRDA (land monetisation)","type":"State Govt","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Worli","Worli Sea Face"],"constituencies":["Worli"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-worli-dairy-land-set-for-redevelopment-into-commercial-financial-hub","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-09-28","claim":"15.8-acre site; MMRDA sole owner and Special Planning Authority; commercial-financial hub; aquarium/marine institute plans may be dropped; objections invited"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.0055,"lng":72.814},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-13","name":"Ramabai Ambedkar Nagar and Kamraj Nagar slum redevelopment, Ghatkopar East","shortName":"Ramabai Nagar redevelopment","summary":"MMRDA's first slum rehabilitation project covers about 32-33 hectares in Ramabai Ambedkar Nagar and Kamraj Nagar, Ghatkopar East, near the Eastern Express Highway. It is planned in four phases with the SRA as planning authority, and the cleared land will let MMRDA extend the Eastern Freeway. CM Fadnavis laid the foundation stone on 14 October 2025 and promised keys to the first-phase flats within two years. In February 2026 FPJ reported that Phase 1 construction would begin only after environmental clearance, which MMRDA had applied for, while the SRA relocated the remaining residents.","sector":"Housing","agency":"MMRDA","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":8498,"revised":null,"note":"Total project Rs 8,498 crore (FPJ, May 2025). The phase-1 contract with B.G. Shirke is Rs 1,299 crore (FPJ, Oct 2025)."},"funders":[{"name":"MMRDA (institutional loans)","type":"State Govt","amount":null,"note":"Rs 3,916 crore of institutional loans planned; first tranche Rs 1,500 crore from Bank of Maharashtra (FPJ, May 2025)"}],"contractor":"B.G. Shirke Construction Technology (phase 1)","startDate":"2025-10-14","targetDate":"2027-10","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Ramabai Ambedkar Nagar","Kamraj Nagar","Ghatkopar East","Eastern Express Highway"],"constituencies":["Ghatkopar East"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/maharashtra-cm-devendra-fadnavis-his-deputies-perform-bhoomipujan-for-ramabai-ambedkar-kamraj-nagar-redevelopment","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-10-14","claim":"Bhoomipujan held; BG Shirke phase-1 contractor; MMRDA executes with SRA; 32 ha; keys within two years"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-mmrda-secures-1500-crore-loan-from-bank-of-maharashtra-for-8498-crore-ramabai-ambedkar-nagar-kamraj-nagar-sra-project","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-05-20","claim":"Total Rs 8,498 crore; Rs 1,500 crore loan from Bank of Maharashtra; 33.15 ha; four phases; 14,500 eligible families"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-mmrda-seeks-moef-clearance-for-ramabai-ambedkar-nagar-redevelopment-as-sra-begins-relocation-drive","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-02-12","claim":"MMRDA sought MoEF clearance; Phase 1 to begin after approval; land needed to extend Eastern Freeway; 31.83 ha; Rs 8,498 crore via institutional loans"},{"url":"https://swarajyamag.com/amp/story/infrastructure/mumbai-makeover-mmrda-and-sra-to-redevelop-ghatkopar-slums-also-paving-way-for-eastern-freeway-extension-till-thane","title":"Swarajya","date":"2024-03-06","claim":"MMRDA-SRA redevelopment clears land for Eastern Freeway extension; 33.15 ha"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.08,"lng":72.915},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-14","name":"Gateway of India comprehensive conservation","shortName":"Gateway of India restoration","summary":"The Maharashtra Archaeology Department began a Rs 7 crore conservation of the Gateway of India in 2023, its first large-scale restoration since minor repairs in 2007. The work covers cleaning, re-plastering, protective chemical coatings, dome treatment, new doors, windows and cast-iron railings, and paving. An undated Mumbai Live report put it at about 30% complete with a February 2025 target. No completion has been reported.","sector":"Heritage & public spaces","agency":"Directorate of Archaeology & Museums, Maharashtra","status":"Delayed","progress":30,"cost":{"original":7,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"Government of Maharashtra","type":"State Govt","amount":7}],"contractor":null,"startDate":"2023","targetDate":"2025-02","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Apollo Bunder","Colaba"],"constituencies":["Colaba"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.mumbailive.com/en/infrastructure/gateway-conservation-project-to-be-completed-by-feb-2025-86781","title":"Mumbai Live","date":null,"claim":"Rs 7 crore project launched in 2023 by the state archaeology department; ~30% complete; target February 2025; first large-scale restoration since minor repairs in 2007; scope of works"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.922,"lng":72.8347},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-15","name":"Crawford Market (Mahatma Jyotiba Phule Mandai) redevelopment, Phase 2","shortName":"Crawford Market Phase 2","summary":"After the heritage market hall was restored from 2015 to 2018 (Phase 1), the BMC built new blocks for fish and mutton vendors in Phase 2, which had been stalled until the Supreme Court ruled for the BMC in 2019. It is also building a one-acre open plaza and basement parking. The May 2022 deadline was missed. In September 2025 the completed blocks had waited a year for an Occupation Certificate, and the BMC said full readiness would take at least 18 more months. In January 2026, after a Bombay High Court order, 37 wholesale fish traders from Dadar were moved temporarily into the basement of Block 3, which still had no Occupation Certificate.","sector":"Heritage & public spaces","agency":"BMC","status":"Delayed","progress":null,"cost":{"original":304.64,"revised":null,"note":"Total estimated cost of Rs 304.64 crore (FPJ, Mar 2020)."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":"2022-05","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"Phase 2 was halted by a court challenge from market vendors until the Supreme Court ruled for the BMC in 2019 (FPJ). Since completion, the new blocks have awaited an Occupation Certificate; an activist attributed this to the building sitting on a Development Plan road. The plaza and parking work was still under way in September 2025 (FPJ).","areas":["Crawford Market","Lokmanya Tilak Marg"],"constituencies":[],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-one-year-after-completion-crawford-markets-redeveloped-building-for-fish-vendors-awaits-oc-from-bmc","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-09-26","claim":"Blocks 3 and 4 complete but awaiting OC; plaza and basement parking ongoing; full readiness 1.5 years; Phase 1 2015-2018; architect Abha Narain Lambah"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/supreme-court-clears-path-for-crawford-market-redevelopment","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2019-05-29","claim":"Supreme Court ruled in BMC's favour on Phase II after vendors' challenge halted work; Phase 1 began Sept 2014"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-swanky-crawford-market-to-be-ready-by-may-2022","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2020-03-09","claim":"Deadline May 2022; total estimated cost Rs 304.64 crore; SC dismissed Crawford Market Association SLP in April 2019"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-fish-traders-from-dadar-shifted-to-crawford-market-after-bombay-high-court-order","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-01-23","claim":"37 Dadar fish traders moved temporarily to Block 3 basement after HC order; building yet to get OC"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-csm-fish-market-association-demands-cancellation-of-loa-to-ava-developer-firm-on-not-relocating-to-crawford-market-building","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-10-15","claim":"Building ready but OC pending since 2024 per architect; CSM fish vendors refuse permanent relocation"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.9474,"lng":72.8343},"statusUnchecked":true,"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-16","name":"Banganga Tank precinct restoration, Walkeshwar","shortName":"Banganga restoration","summary":"The BMC and the GSB Temple Trust are carrying out a phased restoration of the Banganga Tank precinct at Walkeshwar, estimated at about Rs 12 crore. Phase 1 covers restoring the steps and removing encroachments. In June 2024 a contractor used an excavator despite a ban and damaged the heritage steps. The BMC terminated the contract and retendered the work. The deadline was March 2025. A 15-foot section of a compound wall collapsed on 25 May 2025, when Phase 1 was still in progress, and the BMC is repairing it separately.","sector":"Heritage & public spaces","agency":"BMC","status":"Delayed","progress":null,"cost":{"original":12,"revised":null,"note":"Estimated Rs 12 crore (FPJ, May 2024). The BMC had received Rs 5 crore from the state Tourism Department (FPJ, Sept 2024)."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null},{"name":"Government of Maharashtra (Tourism Department)","type":"State Govt","amount":5}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":"2025-03","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"In June 2024 the contractor used an excavator for desilting despite a ban, damaged the heritage steps and sublet work without approval. The BMC terminated the contract and retendered, and FPJ reported that progress slowed (Sept 2024).","areas":["Walkeshwar","Malabar Hill"],"constituencies":["Malabar Hill"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-bmc-plans-urgent-repairs-after-banganga-tank-wall-collapse-at-heritage-site","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-06-13","claim":"Phased restoration by BMC and GSB Temple Trust begun in 2024 is ongoing; wall collapse repair is separate"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-revamps-banganga-tank-restoration-plan-after-contractor-controversy-splits-work-into-3-phases","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2024-09-24","claim":"Contract terminated after excavator damaged steps on 24 June; retendered; Rs 5 crore from Tourism Dept; deadline March 2025"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-begins-malabar-hills-banganga-tank-restoration-project-into-3-phases","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2024-05-02","claim":"Rs 12 crore estimate; three phases; launched in 2023"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/amp/mumbai/mumbai-rains-15-foot-wall-collapses-at-banganga-tank-heritage-site-joint-inspection-by-bmc-archaeology-dept-and-temple-trust-planned","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-05-26","claim":"Wall collapsed 25 May 2025; Phase 1 (step restoration, encroachment removal) in progress"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.9455,"lng":72.7945},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-17","name":"Asiatic Society Town Hall (State Central Library) conservation and repairs","shortName":"Asiatic Library repairs","summary":"By June 2026 the state PWD had sanctioned Rs 5.63 crore for 12 conservation and repair works at the Grade-I heritage Town Hall at Horniman Circle, home of the Asiatic Society library. The work covers structural repairs, plaster, ceilings, original doors, windows and cupboards, flooring, and waterproofing and moisture control for the basement book collection. The government's target was July 2026, and no completion has been reported.","sector":"Heritage & public spaces","agency":"PWD Maharashtra","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":5.63,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"Government of Maharashtra (PWD)","type":"State Govt","amount":5.63}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":"2026-07","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Horniman Circle","Fort"],"constituencies":["Colaba"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-heritage-update-maharashtra-govt-sanctions-563-crore-to-restore-historic-asiatic-library-building","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-06-30","claim":"PWD sanctioned Rs 5.63 crore for 12 works; scope listed; target July 2026"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.9318,"lng":72.8361},"statusUnchecked":true,"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-18","name":"Mahim Fort conservation and precinct rejuvenation","shortName":"Mahim Fort restoration","summary":"The BMC cleared the encroachments around the 800-year-old Mahim Fort and moved 275 eligible hutment dwellers into rehabilitation tenements in Kurla and Malad. On 18 June 2026 it signed an MoU with the Customs Department, which owns the fort. The Rs 20 crore conservation would bring structural repairs, excavation of a historic well, a pedestrian walkway in the precinct and protective works, over about two years.","sector":"Heritage & public spaces","agency":"BMC","status":"Not started","progress":null,"cost":{"original":20,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":"2028-06","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"The BMC began restoration efforts in 2021, but progress was limited because the fort was heavily encroached and is owned by the Union Customs Department, with which a handover had to be arranged (FPJ, Oct 2025).","areas":["Mahim","Mahim Koliwada"],"constituencies":["Mahim"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-heritage-revival-bmc-customs-sign-mou-to-restore-800-year-old-mahim-fort-at-20-crore-cost","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-06-19","claim":"MoU signed 18 June 2026 with Customs; Rs 20 crore; scope; completion within two years; ~275 hutment dwellers rehabilitated"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-restoration-of-800-year-old-mahim-fort-gains-momentum-bmc-coordinates-handover-with-customs-department-video","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-10-09","claim":"BMC launched restoration efforts in 2021 with limited progress; fort owned by Customs; handover being coordinated; heavily encroached"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.043,"lng":72.837},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-19","name":"Hutatma Chowk underground robotic parking","shortName":"Hutatma Chowk parking","summary":"This robotic parking facility at Hutatma Chowk (Apsara) has four underground levels for 176 cars and 18 two-wheelers, and its contract was awarded at Rs 69.54 crore. It is one of four BMC robotic parking towers worth Rs 504.19 crore together. Ground was broken on 5 March 2025. The next day civic activist Kamlakar Shenoy wrote to the BMC alleging financial irregularities and tender manipulation and asking for work to stop. The BMC said it would show him the project's approvals.","sector":"Roads & bridges","agency":"BMC","status":"In progress","progress":null,"cost":{"original":69.54,"revised":null,"note":"Contract value Rs 69.54 crore (FPJ, Nov 2024); about Rs 70 crore at groundbreaking (FPJ, Mar 2025). The four towers (Worli, Mumbadevi, Matunga, Hutatma Chowk) total Rs 504.19 crore."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":"2025-03-05","targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Hutatma Chowk","Fort"],"constituencies":["Colaba"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-infrastructure-news-bmc-begins-work-on-multi-level-robotic-parking-tower-at-hutatma-chowk-aims-to-ease-congestion","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-03-05","claim":"Groundbreaking held; Rs 70 crore; 194 cars; four underground levels; Rs 504.19 crore for all BMC parking projects"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-bmcs-multi-level-robotic-parking-towers-to-solve-citys-parking-crisis-with-504-crore-project","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2024-11-29","claim":"Hutatma Chowk (Apsara): four underground floors, 176 cars and 18 two-wheelers, contract Rs 69.54 crore; four towers total Rs 504.19 crore"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-activist-alleges-financial-irregularities-in-bmcs-504-crore-multi-level-robotic-parking-tower-at-hutatma-chowk-demands-fir-against-officials-firms","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-03-06","claim":"Activist Kamlakar Shenoy alleged financial irregularities and tender manipulation, sought FIR and halt"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.933,"lng":72.8325},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-20","name":"Kala Ghoda precinct development Phase 2 (pedestrian plaza and underground parking)","shortName":"Kala Ghoda Phase 2","summary":"Phase 2 would redo five roads around Kala Ghoda, create a pedestrian plaza outside Rhythm House and make the road outside Jehangir Art Gallery two-way. Phase 2B would turn the existing Kala Ghoda parking into an underground car park. The BMC approved the plans in September 2025, but tendering waits for other agencies' approvals.","sector":"Heritage & public spaces","agency":"BMC","status":"Not started","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null,"note":"Phase 2A estimated at Rs 12 crore, per former corporator Makarand Narwekar."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Kala Ghoda","Fort","M.G. Road","K. Dubash Marg"],"constituencies":["Colaba"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-phase-2-of-kala-ghoda-precinct-development-gets-bmc-approval","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-09-15","claim":"BMC approved Phase 2 plans (by UDA); five roads; plaza; Phase 2B underground parking; tender after other approvals; Phase 1 nearing completion"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.928,"lng":72.832},"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-21","name":"New Mumbai Fire Brigade stations (Kandivali, Kanjurmarg, Santacruz, Chembur, Tilak Nagar, Coastal Road)","shortName":"New fire stations","summary":"The BMC is adding full-size fire stations under the 2014-34 Development Plan. Stations at Thakur Village (Kandivali East) and LBS Marg (Kanjurmarg West) have been completed. Juhu Tara Road (Santacruz), Mahul Road (Chembur) and Tilak Nagar are to be taken up, and two stations are planned on the Coastal Road.","sector":"Other","agency":"BMC (Mumbai Fire Brigade)","status":"Partially open","progress":null,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null,"note":"No per-station costs given. Fire brigade capital budgets were Rs 227.07 crore in 2023-24 and about Rs 261 crore in 2025-26."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":"2023-12","revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":"Space constraints, pending approvals from the mechanical engineering department, and a site change at Chembur to save 128 trees (FPJ, May 2023).","areas":["Thakur Village, Kandivali East","LBS Marg, Kanjurmarg West","Juhu Tara Road, Santacruz West","Mahul Road, Chembur","Tilak Nagar","Coastal Road"],"constituencies":[],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.mumbailive.com/en/civic/seven-new-fire-stations-in-mumbai-centers-at-kandivali-and-kanjurmarg-completed-87666","title":"Mumbai Live","date":null,"claim":"Kandivali (Thakur Village) and Kanjurmarg (LBS Marg) stations completed; Santacruz, Chembur, Tilak Nagar to be taken up; two Coastal Road stations planned"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-faces-delay-in-construction-of-new-fire-stations-only-one-expected-to-be-operational-by-end-of-year","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2023-05-14","claim":"Kandivali target December 2023, Kanjurmarg 2024; delay reasons; Rs 227.07 crore in 2023-24"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-addition-of-5-new-fire-stations-7-sewage-plants-in-suburbs-announces-municipal-commissioner-bhushan-gagrani","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2024-08-16","claim":"Commissioner: Thakur Village (Kandivali E) and LBS Road (Kanjurmarg W) stations under construction, to be completed soon; Juhu Tara Road, Mahul Road, Tilak Nagar to start soon"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.209,"lng":72.875},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-22","name":"Chandivali full-fledged fire station","shortName":"Chandivali fire station","summary":"This fire station will replace the mini station at Chandivali, near the Lake Home project. In June 2026 the BMC Standing Committee approved a Rs 22.73 crore contract with M.M. Enterprises for a ground-plus-six-storey station building with staff quarters and a ground-plus-four-storey drill tower. Work was to begin soon, with completion expected within two years of the start.","sector":"Other","agency":"BMC (Mumbai Fire Brigade)","status":"Not started","progress":null,"cost":{"original":22.73,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":22.73}],"contractor":"M.M. Enterprises","startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Chandivali","Powai"],"constituencies":["Chandivali"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-infra-update-bmc-approves-2273-crore-chandivali-fire-station-project-to-boost-emergency-response","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-06-15","claim":"Rs 22.73 crore; contractor M.M. Enterprises; G+6 station and G+4 drill tower; two-year completion"},{"url":"https://www.mumbailive.com/en/civic/chandivali-to-get-full-fledged-fire-station-to-cut-emergency-response-time-in-powai-saki-naka-93211","title":"Mumbai Live","date":null,"claim":"Rs 22.73 crore approved by Standing Committee; M.M. Enterprises; work set to begin soon; completion within two years of start"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.12,"lng":72.896},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-23","name":"Delisle Road bridge (Lower Parel road over bridge) reconstruction","shortName":"Delisle bridge","summary":"The Delisle Road bridge over the Western Railway tracks at Lower Parel was shut in 2018 after an IIT Bombay report and demolished in February 2019. Western Railway rebuilt the span over the tracks, launching its girders in 2022, and the BMC rebuilt the approaches. One arm opened on 1 June 2023, the second on 18 September, and the full bridge on 23 November 2023.","sector":"Roads & bridges","agency":"BMC & Western Railway","status":"Completed","progress":100,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null,"note":"No total published. Western Railway's reconstruction contract was Rs 87 crore (Feb 2019) and the BMC's approach-road contract Rs 138 crore (Jan 2020) (FPJ, Oct 2023). Delays raised the cost by Rs 14 crore (FPJ, Sept 2023)."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null},{"name":"Indian Railways (Western Railway)","type":"Central Govt","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":"2019-09","targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":"2023-11-23","delayReason":"Closed for over five years. FPJ (Oct 2023) attributed the final missed deadlines to slow concrete setting, a water-tanker strike and a shortage of steel.","areas":["Lower Parel","N.M. Joshi Marg","Ganpatrao Kadam Marg"],"constituencies":["Worli"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/amp/mumbai/mumbai-news-delisle-bridge-set-for-full-inauguration-after-five-years-of-closure","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2023-11-22","claim":"Closed 2018, demolished Feb 2019; first arm opened June, second 18 Sept; full opening 23 Nov 2023; BMC worked on its portion from Feb 2020"},{"url":"https://theprint.in/india/mumbai-delisle-bridge-partially-opens-for-motorists-reconstruction-work-to-be-completed-by-july-end/1606847","title":"ThePrint (PTI)","date":"2023-06-01","claim":"Shut in 2018 on IIT Bombay audit; one arm opened 1 June 2023; girder launch the hardest part; WR handed over to BMC Oct 2022"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-news-delislebridgeto-open-by-diwali-after-missed-deadlines","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2023-10-12","claim":"Missed deadlines due to slow concrete setting, water tanker strike, steel shortage; Rs 87 crore railway contract (Feb 2019), Rs 138 crore BMC approach contract (Jan 2020)"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/amp/mumbai/mumbai-news-delay-in-5-city-projects-escalates-cost-by-2676-crore","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2023-09-25","claim":"Delisle bridge cost rose by Rs 14 crore due to delays"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.996,"lng":72.83},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-24","name":"Chheda Nagar junction traffic improvement (flyovers), Ghatkopar–Chembur","shortName":"Chheda Nagar flyovers","summary":"This Rs 249 crore MMRDA project, begun in 2017, builds three flyovers and a vehicle subway at Chheda Nagar junction to make traffic between the Eastern Express Highway, SCLR and the Ghatkopar–Mankhurd Link Road signal-free. The Chheda Nagar–SCLR flyover opened on 14 March 2022 and a 1.23 km flyover from the GMLR towards Thane opened in April 2023, when a roughly 600 m south-north flyover was still due. CM Eknath Shinde opened another flyover, signposted towards Vikhroli and Thane, on 12 October 2024. FPJ's report of that opening also says a south-north flyover from Amar Mahal towards Vikhroli was 95% complete, so it is unclear from approved sources whether any part remains unopened.","sector":"Roads & bridges","agency":"MMRDA","status":"Partially open","progress":null,"cost":{"original":249,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"MMRDA","type":"State Govt","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":"2017","targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Chheda Nagar","Ghatkopar East","Chembur","Amar Mahal","Eastern Express Highway"],"constituencies":["Chembur"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-cm-eknath-shinde-inaugurates-much-awaited-chedda-nagar-flyover-on-eastern-express-highway-to-ease-traffic-congestion","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2024-10-12","claim":"Opened 12 Oct 2024; Rs 249 crore project begun 2017 by MMRDA; Amar Mahal–Vikhroli south-north flyover 95% complete"},{"url":"https://mumbailive.com/en/infrastructure/mmrda-finally-opens-up-chheda-nagar-sclr-flyover-for-vehicle-use-72162","title":"Mumbai Live","date":null,"claim":"Chheda Nagar–SCLR flyover opened Monday 14 March (year not printed; 2022 per other reports); three flyovers cost Rs 249 crore together"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/amp/mumbai/mumbai-cm-inaugurates-flyover-at-chheda-nagar-junction-to-provide-signal-free-travel-for-commuters","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2023-04-13","claim":"1.23 km GMLR–EEH (Thane) flyover opened; second of three flyovers and a subway; 600 m south-north flyover due in December"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.0662,"lng":72.91},"statusUnchecked":true,"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-25","name":"Dr Bhau Daji Lad Museum restoration, Byculla","shortName":"Bhau Daji Lad Museum","summary":"The BMC restored the Dr Bhau Daji Lad Museum, which the CM called Maharashtra's oldest museum, inside Jijamata Udyan in Byculla, at a cost of Rs 3 crore. The tendered work covered the tile roof and ornamental ceiling, terrace waterproofing, the facade, wooden doors and windows, plastering and painting, and anti-termite treatment. The museum had been shut for four years, first for COVID-19 and then for the works. CM Fadnavis reopened it on 8 January 2025.","sector":"Heritage & public spaces","agency":"BMC","status":"Completed","progress":100,"cost":{"original":3,"revised":null,"note":"Rs 3 crore spent by the BMC (ThePrint/PTI, Jan 2025); about Rs 3 crore at tender (FPJ, Dec 2022)."},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":3}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":"2025-01-08","delayReason":null,"areas":["Byculla","Jijamata Udyan"],"constituencies":["Byculla"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://theprint.in/india/revamped-bhau-daji-lad-museum-reopens-after-four-years/2436402","title":"ThePrint (PTI)","date":"2025-01-08","claim":"CM inaugurated renovated museum on 8 Jan 2025; BMC spent Rs 3 crore; shut for four years"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/amp/mumbai/mumbai-dr-bhau-daji-lad-museum-to-undergo-rs3cr-revamp","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2022-12-05","claim":"BMC tender for ~Rs 3 crore revamp: tile roof, ceiling, terrace waterproofing, facade, doors and windows, plastering, anti-termite; 18 months"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.979,"lng":72.834},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-26","name":"Bandra East skywalk (station to Bandra Court, BKC and Western Express Highway)","shortName":"Bandra East skywalk","summary":"A 680 m skywalk now links Bandra East station with Bandra Court, the Collector's office, MHADA, BKC and the Western Express Highway, replacing an older skywalk dismantled in 2021 for a Kalanagar flyover arm. The BMC oversaw the work. It has two escalators and 14 CCTV cameras. Guardian Minister Ashish Shelar opened it on 26 January 2026, a few days after Western Railway approved access from its foot overbridge.","sector":"Roads & bridges","agency":"BMC","status":"Completed","progress":100,"cost":{"original":null,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":"2026-01-26","delayReason":null,"areas":["Bandra East","Bandra Court","BKC","Western Express Highway"],"constituencies":["Vandre East"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.mumbailive.com/en/civic/new-680-meter-skywalk-in-bandra-east-finally-reopens-for-public-91506","title":"Mumbai Live","date":"2026-01-26","claim":"680 m, 5.4 m wide; opened Monday 26 January 2026 by Ashish Shelar; links station, court, BKC, MHADA, WEH; two escalators, 14 CCTV"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-infra-news-680-metre-bandra-east-skywalk-linking-court-bkc-and-weh-opens-after-5-years-video","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-01-27","claim":"Opened 26 Jan 2026 by Ashish Shelar; 680 m; older skywalk dismantled in 2021 for Kalanagar flyover arm; two escalators, 14 CCTV"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.056,"lng":72.842},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-27","name":"Kurla–BKC skywalk (Sitaram Bhairu Marg, across LBS Road)","shortName":"Kurla–BKC skywalk","summary":"This Rs 14.36 crore skywalk across LBS Road in Kurla West, from Taximen Colony to Shrikrishna Chowk, links Kurla with BKC. It was approved in August 2021 with an 18-month deadline. After about five years of delays it was expected to open in June 2026, with escalators still pending. No opening has been confirmed.","sector":"Roads & bridges","agency":"BMC","status":"Delayed","progress":null,"cost":{"original":14.36,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"BMC (own funds)","type":"Municipal","amount":null}],"contractor":null,"startDate":"2021-08","targetDate":"2023-04","revisedTargetDate":"2026-06","completedDate":null,"delayReason":"Underground utilities (high-tension cables, a Mahanagar Gas pipeline, a storm drain and a major water main) and encroachments.","areas":["Kurla West","Taximen Colony","LBS Road","BKC"],"constituencies":["Kurla"],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-after-5-year-delay-kurlabkc-skywalk-nears-completion-set-to-open-in-june","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-05-30","claim":"Rs 14.36 crore; approved Aug 2021, 18-month deadline; deadlines slipped April 2023 → April 2024 → March 2026; expected first week of June 2026; delay reasons"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":19.071,"lng":72.877},"statusUnchecked":true,"evidence":"single","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-28","name":"Mahalaxmi travelator skywalk linking Metro 3, Monorail and Mahalaxmi station","shortName":"Mahalaxmi travelator skywalk","summary":"MMRDA is building Mumbai's first skywalk with travelators at Mahalaxmi. The 283 m, 11 m wide bridge has six travelators totalling 176 m and is meant to link the Sant Gadge Maharaj Chowk Monorail station with Mahalaxmi suburban station and Metro Line 3. Mumbai Live reported that the design was shortened to end at Jacob Circle, about 200 m from the Metro station. It is designed for about 4,500 passengers an hour and was about 90% complete in July 2026.","sector":"Roads & bridges","agency":"MMRDA","status":"In progress","progress":90,"cost":{"original":82.66,"revised":null,"note":"Work order of Rs 82.66 crore including GST, with a 12-month execution period (Niraj Cement Structurals stock-exchange filing, 4 Dec 2025)."},"funders":[{"name":"MMRDA","type":"State Govt","amount":null}],"contractor":"Niraj Cement Structurals Ltd (JV)","startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Mahalaxmi","Jacob Circle (Sant Gadge Maharaj Chowk)"],"constituencies":[],"citywide":false,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-mahalaxmi-multimodal-hub-nears-completion-travelator-to-handle-4500-passengers-an-hour","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-07-26","claim":"MMRDA: ~90% complete; 283 m, 11 m wide; six travelators totalling 176 m; links Monorail, Metro 3 and Mahalaxmi station; 4,500 passengers/hour"},{"url":"https://www.mumbailive.com/en/infrastructure/mumbais-first-travelator-skywalk-connecting-mumbai-monorail-and-mahalakshmi-metro-station-shortened-92869","title":"Mumbai Live","date":null,"claim":"Shortened from 384 m; ends at Jacob Circle ~200 m from Metro station; JV led by Niraj Cement Structurals, Rs 82.66 crore"},{"url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/NIRAJ_04122025154722_Intimation_MMRDA.pdf","title":"Niraj Cement Structurals Ltd, Regulation 30 disclosure to NSE/BSE","date":"2025-12-04","claim":"MMRDA work order for connectivity from SGMC monorail station to Mahalaxmi metro and suburban station through FOB with travellator; Rs 82.66 crore incl. GST; 12 months"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.9825,"lng":72.824},"evidence":"official","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"},
    {"id":"MORE-29","name":"Mumbai Police housing township (redevelopment of police colonies)","shortName":"Police housing township","summary":"In January 2026 the state Cabinet cleared a Rs 20,000 crore plan to redevelop existing police colonies across Mumbai into nearly 45,000 quarters for police personnel. MSIDC is the nodal agency for the PWD and can raise government-guaranteed loans for 70% of the cost, and an initial Rs 100 crore grant pays for feasibility studies. No colonies or construction dates have been announced.","sector":"Housing","agency":"MSIDC (for PWD Maharashtra)","status":"Not started","progress":null,"cost":{"original":20000,"revised":null},"funders":[{"name":"Government of Maharashtra","type":"State Govt","amount":null,"note":"30% of cost; initial Rs 100 crore grant"},{"name":"Institutional loans (government-guaranteed)","type":"Private / PPP","amount":null,"note":"70% of cost"}],"contractor":null,"startDate":null,"targetDate":null,"revisedTargetDate":null,"completedDate":null,"delayReason":null,"areas":["Police colonies across Mumbai"],"constituencies":[],"citywide":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/maharashtra-cabinet-clears-20000-crore-housing-township-for-mumbai-police-personnel","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2026-01-18","claim":"Cabinet cleared Rs 20,000 crore; nearly 45,000 quarters in existing colonies; MSIDC nodal agency for PWD; state 30%, 70% loans with govt guarantee; Rs 100 crore initial grant"},{"url":"https://www.mumbailive.com/en/infrastructure/20000-crore-housing-township-cleared-to-upgrade-mumbai-police-residences-91410","title":"Mumbai Live","date":null,"claim":"Nearly 45,000 units by redeveloping existing police colonies; MSIDC nodal agency for PWD; no colonies named"},{"url":"https://www.freepressjournal.in/mumbai/mumbai-police-housing-crisis-maharashtra-govt-to-redevelop-75-plots-build-40000-new-residential-units","title":"Free Press Journal","date":"2025-10-11","claim":"Earlier plan: 75 plots, 40,000 new units; MSIDC MD member-secretary of high-level panel"}],"lastVerified":"2026-11-20","location":{"lat":18.947,"lng":72.834},"evidence":"multiple","recheckedAt":"2026-11-20"}
